I think that the obvious solution is kicking.  Kicking your pet should not be
interpreted by the game as an attack against your pet, but rather an attempt
to motivate it to get out of your way.  Thus it should not do any hit-point
damage to your pet and it should not cause you to loose any luck or anger
dieties.

EX:

    ###f@

(Your command to the game): ^Dh


You kick your kitten  --more--

Your kitten lets out a yowl!  --more--



    ###@f



Kicking pets seems to me to be the natural method of pet control
in the dungeons of nethack.  These kicks are not mean-spirited kicks
that would injure.  They are just a poke in the ribs to get the pet's
attention.

